<title>UK: Stagecoach sees Swebus deal agreed next week.</title>
<headline>Stagecoach sees Swebus deal agreed next week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bus and passenger rail operator Stagecoach Holdings Plc said on Wednesday that its negotiations to acquire Swedish long distance bus operator Swebus AB were set to lead to a signed agreement next week. Four weeks ago Stagecoach said it had agreed the deal in principle, and it expected to pay 110 million stg-plus for the firm, with Swebus' current owner, the state railway company.</p>
<p>&quot;The directors report that negotiations with the vendors of Swebus AB are proceeding and they expect an agreement (conditional on shareholder approval) will be signed next week,&quot; Stagecoach said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
